&#34;This new senior deduction would be set at $4,000 per individual in the House bill or at $6,000 per individual in the Senate bill.

The deduction would phase out at a 4 percent rate in the House bill when modified adjusted gross income (adjusted gross income plus any tax-exempt interest income) exceeds $75,000 for single filers and $150,000 for joint filers. The Senate bill accelerates the phaseout, increasing it to 6 percent. In both bills, the deduction would be fully phased out at $175,000 for single filers and $250,000 for joint filers.&#34;

